# .claude/ is local state - settings.local.json is per-machine, worktrees/
# is scratch - with exceptions. agents/ holds the operational brief for
# working on this fork: the test invocation and its symlink trap, the doc
# cache path, the cohort ownership split, and the adversarial-audit shapes.
# scripts/ holds small executable machinery an orchestrating agent or the
# maintainer runs directly (e.g. checking a background subagent's progress
# without reading its full transcript into context) - the same "make it a
# mechanism, not prose" reasoning as skills/, just not shaped as a skill.
#
# HANDOFF.md used to carry that material and was tracked. Retiring it
# (099193d189) moved the work items to the tracker, which was right, and
# moved the operational half here, which left the only written record of
# how to work on this repository untracked on one machine - invisible to a
# fresh clone (issue #165).
#
# The exclusion is written as /.claude/* rather than /.claude/, because git
# does not descend into an excluded directory and a ! rule beneath one
# never matches.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/skills/
!/.claude/scripts/

# tools/<name> binaries: `go build ./tools/<name>` (or `go build
# ./tools/<name>/...`), run from the repo root with no -o, drops a
# same-named binary here — one entry per tools/ subdirectory that is a
# package main, so an accidental `go build`/`go install` from the repo
# root never lands a multi-megabyte binary in `git status` again (issue:
# an ~80MB tools/estate-gen build got committed by accident and had to be
# stripped back out of a merge).
/admission-pipeline
/armtypes-gen
/aws-paginators-gen
/azurerm-id-gen
/azurerm-tags-gen
/ci-gate
/cloudcontrol-probe
/contribute
/corpus-fetch
/corpus-gen
/credential-sweep
/estate-gen
/estate-plan
/estate-types
/find-dep-upgrades
/floci-capability-gen
/forkdiff-gen
/gcp-row-gen
/gotest-record
/harness-gen
/iamref-gen
/largeset-gen
/importdocs-gen
/importer-probe
/limits-gen
/mapping-gen
/merge-guard
/modcompat
/modcompat-gen
/oracle-bump-report
/protobuf-compile
/provider-bump-report
/readiness-gen
/refusal-probe
/registry-gen
/row-gen
/scenario-estate
/selected-go-version
/statpages
/substrates-gen
/survey-gen
/tagverbs-gen
/terralith-gen
/toggles-gen
/wo-sweep

# The #102 corpus: third-party configurations pinned in live/corpus-manifest.json
# and materialized by tools/corpus-fetch. Reproducible from the pins, so not
# committed - vendoring it would add weight and third-party licenses for no
# measurement value.
# No trailing slash: agents working in git worktrees symlink the corpus in
# rather than re-fetching 250 repositories, and a directory pattern does not
# match a symlink. Three hit this in one session and each caught it by hand
# before committing; the fourth would not have.
/.corpus

# tools/gauntlet: the binary (same rule as every tools/ subdirectory above)
# and the per-estate run logs it captures.
/gauntlet
/live/gauntlet/logs/

# CI gate scratch files a worker leaves in its worktree; never tracked.
# ci.meta is #519's run-identity sidecar (HEAD sha, start/end timestamps)
# that scripts/ci-gate.sh writes beside ci.rc/ci.out so a reader can tell a
# fresh gate from a stale one; ci.meta.tmp is its write-then-rename staging
# file, briefly present mid-write.
ci.out
ci.rc
ci.meta
ci.meta.tmp
gate.launch.log

# worker scratch repros and local record stores never belong in the repo
.repro/
.tofu-records/

# site/ (#2092): the Astro build and its dependencies, never tracked.
# dist/ above already matches the build; both are named here so moving or
# narrowing that rule cannot start tracking them. site/public/ is tracked:
# it holds the logo files the build copies as they are.
/site/node_modules/
/site/dist/
/site/.astro/
